er or conflict, depending on the nature of the march and the reactions it provokes. [Data: Entities (5), Relationships (37, 38, 39, 40, 41,+more)]\"\n        }},\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Harmony Assembly's role in the community\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Harmony Assembly is another key entity in this community, being the organizer of the march at Verdant Oasis Plaza. The nature of Harmony Assembly and its march could be a potential source of threat, depending on their objectives and the reactions they provoke. The relationship between Harmony Assembly and the plaza is crucial in understanding the dynamics of this community. [Data: Entities(6), Relationships (38, 43)]\"\n        }},\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Unity March as a significant event\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The Unity March is a significant event taking place at Verdant Oasis Plaza. This event is a key factor in the community's dynamics and could be a potential source of threat, depending on the nature of the march and the reactions it provokes. The relationship between the march and the plaza is crucial in understanding the dynamics of this community. [Data: Relationships (39)]\"\n        }},\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Role of Tribune Spotlight\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Tribune Spotlight is reporting on the Unity March taking place in Verdant Oasis Plaza. This suggests that the event has attracted media attention, which could amplify its impact on the community. The role of Tribune Spotlight could be significant in shaping public perception of the event and the entities involved. [Data: Relationships (40)]\"\n        }}\n    ]\n}}\n\n\n# Real Data\n\nUse the following text for your answer. Do not make anything up in your answer.\n\nText:\n-----Entities-----\nhuman_readable_id,title,description,degree\r\n697,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,\"NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL, or parenteral nutrition (PN), is a specialized medical treatment that delivers nutritional support intravenously to patients who are unable to receive adequate nutrition through the gastrointestinal tract. This method is essential for individuals who cannot tolerate enteral nutrition due to various conditions, including severe pancreatitis, chronic intestinal failure, post-operative complications, short bowel syndrome, high-output fistulas, and severe malnutrition requiring surgical intervention.\n\nThe treatment involves the direct administration of a complex mixture of macro and micronutrients into the bloodstream, bypassing the usual processes of eating and digestion. It is particularly vital for pediatric patients, those undergoing chemotherapy or radiotherapy, and individuals with significant nutritional deficiencies, such as those suffering from quilotórax and ascitis quilosa. NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL is indicated when enteral feeding is not possible, insufficient, or contraindicated, and is often utilized in critical care settings to stabilize nutritional status and reduce morbidity and mortality.\n\nParenteral nutrition can be administered through central or peripheral intravenous routes, depending on the patient's condition, and requires careful monitoring to avoid complications such as hyperglycemia and hepatobiliary issues. It is a crucial alternative to enteral nutrition, ensuring that patients who cannot eat or absorb food normally receive the necessary nutrients for recovery and overall health. This method is also used until enteral nutrition can be utilized or when the digestive system is not functional.\n\nIn summary, NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL serves as a critical intervention for patients with gastrointestinal dysfunction or those unable to consume food orally, providing essential nutrients directly into the bloodstream to support their health and recovery.\",438\r\n604,ENFERMEDADES,\"ENFERMEDADES refer to various health conditions that can significantly impact an individual's nutritional needs and treatment. These diseases may coexist with diabetes, influencing the management of the condition and the patient's overall health. Additionally, ENFERMEDADES can affect athletes, often linked to inadequate nutritional practices, which can compromise their health and performance. In children requiring parenteral nutrition, underlying diseases can alter their metabolism and energy requirements, further complicating their nutritional needs. Overall, ENFERMEDADES encompass medical conditions that can adversely affect a patient's nutritional status, highlighting the importance of tailored nutritional interventions in managing these health issues.\",3\r\n5004,HEPATOPATÍA ASOCIADA A NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,\"Liver damage associated with home parenteral nutrition, which can occur due to various factors related to intestinal failure.\",2\r\n2301,QUIMIO,\"QUIMIO refers to chemotherapy, a type of cancer treatment that utilizes drugs to target and kill cancer cells. This treatment method is known to present nutritional challenges for patients undergoing therapy, as the side effects of the drugs can impact their ability to maintain a healthy diet.\",2\r\n7940,TABLA 3,\"\"\"Tabla 3\"\" serves as a comprehensive resource that encompasses various aspects of nutrition and dietary assessment. It outlines the reference intake of vitamins and minerals for adults, providing essential guidelines for nutritional adequacy. Additionally, it presents commercial combinations of nitrogen and glucose solutions specifically designed for hypocaloric peripheral parenteral nutrition, which is crucial for patients requiring specialized dietary support.\n\nFurthermore, \"\"Tabla 3\"\" includes a nutritional assessment based on weight loss percentages over time, allowing for the evaluation of dietary effectiveness and health outcomes. It also details the content of phenylalanine in various foods per 100 grams, which is particularly relevant for individuals managing specific dietary restrictions.\n\nThe table features data from a population study focusing on body mass index (IMC) among men and women aged 45 to 60 years, contributing to a better understanding of nutritional status within this demographic. In addition, \"\"Tabla 3\"\" outlines clinical parameters for monitoring patients receiving parenteral nutrition, ensuring that healthcare providers can effectively track patient progress and nutritional needs.\n\nMoreover, it highlights the main problems encountered when analyzing dietary intake records, which is vital for improving dietary assessments and interventions. Lastly, \"\"Tabla 3\"\" addresses the negative aspects that powdered ingredients may exhibit when in contact with water, emphasizing the importance of formulation stability in nutritional products. Overall, \"\"Tabla 3\"\" is a multifaceted tool that integrates various nutritional data and considerations for both clinical and dietary applications.\",9\r\n4902,AMINOÁCIDOS,\"Aminoácidos are organic compounds that serve as the fundamental building blocks of proteins, playing a crucial role in various bodily functions. They are essential nutrients included in parenteral nutrition solutions to meet the protein needs of patients, particularly those undergoing dialysis or requiring nutritional support. Amino acids are vital for maintaining lean body mass, supporting protein synthesis, and facilitating muscle synthesis and energy production. Additionally, they are important for growth and development, especially in pediatric nutrition. It is noted that specific requirements for amino acids may increase during physical exercise, highlighting their significance in both health and recovery.\",5\r\n1928,B. BALERDI PÉREZ,\"B. Balerdi Pérez is a medical professional with significant contributions to the field of nutrition and trauma care. He co-authored a chapter on polytraumatism and traumatic brain injury, showcasing his expertise in critical medical conditions. Additionally, he has authored several chapters related to parenteral nutrition, including topics on access routes, nutrition for burn patients, and nutrition in cases of renal insufficiency. His work emphasizes the importance of tailored nutritional strategies in various medical scenarios, particularly in critical care settings. Overall, B. Balerdi Pérez's contributions reflect a deep commitment to advancing knowledge in medical nutrition and trauma management.\",4\r\n2221,ENFERMEDAD HEPÁTICA,\"Enfermedad hepática refers to liver disease, a medical condition that encompasses a range of disorders affecting liver function, including cirrhosis and hepatitis. This condition can significantly impact amino acid metabolism and nutritional status, influencing the energy expenditure and nutritional requirements of affected individuals. Careful nutritional management is essential for those with liver disease, as parenteral nutrition can exacerbate the condition and further affect liver function and health.\",4\r\n\n\n-----Relationships-----\nhuman_readable_id,source,target,description,combined_degree\r\n3074,PACIENTE,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,\"The patient is the recipient of parenteral nutrition, a specialized form of nutritional support administered when individuals are unable to utilize their digestive system. This type of nutrition is particularly critical for patients with severe malnutrition or those undergoing treatments such as cancer therapy, where traditional dietary intake is not feasible. The patient's health status plays a significant role in determining the necessity for parenteral nutrition, which is provided to meet their specific nutritional requirements.\n\nParenteral nutrition is typically administered to patients who cannot receive nutrition through the digestive tract, ensuring that their nutritional needs are adequately met. However, patients receiving this form of nutrition are at risk for potential complications, including hyperglycemia. In some cases, patients may receive home parenteral nutrition to manage their nutritional needs effectively, especially in instances of intestinal failure. Overall, parenteral nutrition serves as a vital intervention for patients requiring alternative nutritional support due to their medical conditions.\",984\r\n2599,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,\"NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL and NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL are two distinct methods of providing nutritional support to patients who are unable to consume food orally or utilize their digestive tract effectively. Both approaches are essential for patients with various medical conditions, including those with respiratory issues and those who have undergone gastrectomy. \n\nNUTRICIÓN ENTERAL is generally preferred over NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL due to its lower complication rates, reduced costs, and better outcomes in critically ill patients. It is particularly favored when the digestive tract is functional, such as in cases of severe pancreatitis, where enteral nutrition is the first choice. However, NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL is indicated when enteral nutrition is not tolerated or when the digestive system cannot be used adequately. \n\nBoth methods can be utilized in pediatric care and may be employed in conjunction when enteral nutrition alone is insufficient. Nutritional support can transition from parenteral to enteral as patients adapt and their conditions improve. Overall, the choice between NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL and NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL depends on the specific needs and conditions of the patient, with a general preference for enteral methods when feasible.\",773\r\n473,PACIENTES,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,\"PACIENTES are individuals who may require NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL when enteral nutrition is insufficient or not possible due to various medical complications. This form of nutrition is specifically indicated for patients suffering from severe malnutrition, particularly when enteral nutrition cannot be administered. Patients receiving parenteral nutrition are those who cannot meet their nutritional needs through oral intake or other means, and they may also be recipients of home parenteral nutrition based on their specific medical conditions. Overall, parenteral nutrition serves as a critical alternative for patients who are unable to receive adequate nutrition through enteral routes.\",665\r\n3174,PACIENTE,ENFERMEDADES,\"Patients may have multiple diseases that coexist with diabetes, complicating their treatment and nutritional requirements.\",549\r\n3147,PACIENTE,HEPATOPATÍA ASOCIADA A NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,The patient is at risk of developing liver damage associated with their home parenteral nutrition.,548\r\n3112,PACIENTE,QUIMIO,\"Chemotherapy often leads to nutritional deficiencies in patients, necessitating nutritional support\",548\r\n4607,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,MALNUTRICIÓN,\"NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL is a medical intervention utilized primarily in patients suffering from MALNUTRICIÓN, particularly when these individuals are unable to receive adequate nutrition through enteral methods. This form of nutrition is essential for restoring adequate nutrient levels in patients who cannot absorb nutrients through the gastrointestinal tract or who are unable to receive nutrition enterally for various reasons. The administration of parenteral nutrition is a critical approach to treating malnutrition, ensuring that patients receive the necessary nutrients to support their health and recovery when other nutritional methods are insufficient.\",542\r\n4586,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,NUTRICIÓN ARTIFICIAL,\"NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL and NUTRICIÓN ARTIFICIAL are closely related concepts in the field of nutritional support. NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL refers to a specific method of providing nutrition artificially, particularly in patients who are unable to consume food normally due to various medical conditions. This form of nutrition is utilized when enteral feeding, which involves delivering nutrients directly into the gastrointestinal tract, is not feasible or when the gastrointestinal tract is not functioning properly. \n\nNUTRICIÓN ARTIFICIAL encompasses various methods of nutritional support, including NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL, and is employed in situations where patients require nutritional assistance. Parenteral nutrition is an essential component of the overall management strategy for patients needing artificial nutrition, ensuring that they receive the necessary nutrients when traditional feeding methods are not possible. Thus, both NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL and NUTRICIÓN ARTIFICIAL play critical roles in the care of patients with specific dietary needs.\",531\r\n2918,ESPEN,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,\"ESPEN (European Society for Clinical Nutrition and Metabolism) provides comprehensive guidelines for the use of parenteral nutrition, particularly in situations where enteral feeding is not feasible. These guidelines cover a range of clinical scenarios, including the administration of parenteral nutrition in patients with pancreatitis, liver diseases, and those experiencing intestinal failure. Additionally, ESPEN emphasizes the importance of managing patients who require nutritional support, ensuring that their specific needs are met. The organization also addresses the use of parenteral nutrition in post-surgical patients, highlighting best practices for effective nutritional management in these contexts. Overall, ESPEN's guidelines serve as a critical resource for healthcare professionals involved in the care of patients requiring parenteral nutrition.\",523\r\n4681,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,CALCIO,\"NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL, which refers to the intravenous administration of nutrients, plays a critical role in the care of patients who cannot obtain adequate nutrition through oral means. A key component of this nutritional support is CALCIO (calcium), which is essential for maintaining bone health and supporting various physiological functions. Adequate calcium intake is particularly crucial for patients receiving parenteral nutrition to prevent bone-related issues, especially in pediatric patients who require calcium for proper development.\n\nCalcium is included in parenteral nutrition solutions to meet the body's mineral requirements, and it is recognized as a necessary supplement for these patients. However, the addition of calcium must be done with caution to avoid potential complications. Therefore, healthcare providers closely monitor and adjust calcium levels in patients receiving parenteral nutrition to ensure optimal metabolic health and prevent deficiencies. Overall, calcium is an indispensable mineral in parenteral nutrition, vital for the health and development of patients, particularly children.\",521\r\n4858,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,VITAMINA D,\"NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL refers to a method of providing nutrition to patients intravenously, bypassing the usual process of eating and digestion. In this context, VITAMINA D plays a crucial role, as Vitamin D levels are monitored in patients receiving parenteral nutrition to prevent deficiencies. It has been observed that Vitamin D levels may be insufficient in patients on prolonged parenteral nutrition, highlighting the importance of regular monitoring. Consequently, Vitamin D supplementation is recommended for patients undergoing parenteral nutrition who exhibit specific deficiencies, ensuring that their nutritional needs are adequately met.\",512\r\n930,DESNUTRICIÓN,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,\"Malnutrition is a significant condition that often necessitates the use of parenteral nutrition, particularly in patients who are unable to meet their nutritional requirements through oral or enteral means. This is especially relevant for individuals suffering from liver diseases, where parenteral nutrition serves as a critical intervention to address malnutrition. Patients experiencing malnutrition typically have increased caloric needs, and parenteral nutrition is employed to fulfill these needs effectively. Thus, both \"\"DESNUTRICIÓN\"\" and \"\"NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL\"\" are closely linked, with parenteral nutrition being a vital solution for managing malnutrition in various patient populations.\",512\r\n4802,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,CÁNCER,La nutrición parenteral es necesaria para pacientes con cáncer que tienen insuficiencia intestinal grave,504\r\n4647,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,PROTEÍNAS,\"NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL and PROTEÍNAS are closely related in the context of medical nutrition therapy. Proteins are recognized as a critical component of parenteral nutrition, with specific recommendations for their intake. They play an essential role in the recovery of critically ill patients, as they are necessary for tissue repair and overall recovery. Thus, the inclusion of adequate protein in parenteral nutrition is vital for supporting the health and recovery of patients who are unable to receive nutrition through traditional means.\",495\r\n4655,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,ENFERMEDAD INFLAMATORIA INTESTINAL,\"NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL is a medical intervention utilized when enteral nutrition is not feasible, particularly in patients suffering from ENFERMEDAD INFLAMATORIA INTESTINAL. This form of nutrition is especially important during severe flare-ups of the disease, as it provides essential nutrients directly into the bloodstream, bypassing the gastrointestinal tract. Thus, for individuals with inflammatory bowel disease, parenteral nutrition serves as a critical alternative to ensure adequate nutritional support when traditional methods are inadequate.\",495\r\n4611,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,PANCREATITIS AGUDA,\"NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL is a critical component in the management of PANCREATITIS AGUDA, particularly for patients who are unable to tolerate oral feeding. In cases where enteral nutrition is not viable or fails to meet the energy requirements of the patient, parenteral nutrition becomes necessary. This form of nutritional support is typically utilized during the initial days of treatment for acute pancreatitis, ensuring that patients receive adequate nutrition intravenously when enteral routes are not possible or sufficient. Overall, parenteral nutrition is indicated for the effective management of patients suffering from acute pancreatitis, highlighting its importance in their care.\",492\r\n4650,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,CIRROSIS,\"NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL and CIRROSIS are interconnected in the context of medical treatment. Cirrhosis can develop as a severe complication associated with parenteral nutrition, which is a method of delivering nutrients directly into the bloodstream when a patient is unable to eat by mouth. Parenteral nutrition is specifically reserved for patients with cirrhosis when enteral feeding, or feeding through the gastrointestinal tract, is not feasible. This highlights the critical role of parenteral nutrition in managing the nutritional needs of cirrhosis patients under certain circumstances.\",492\r\n4683,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,MAGNESIO,\"NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL involves the inclusion of MAGNESIO (magnesium), which is an essential component for the proper development and metabolic function of patients, particularly pediatric patients. Magnesium plays a crucial role in various bodily functions and must be monitored and supplemented in parenteral nutrition solutions to prevent deficiencies. Its importance is underscored by the need for careful management in parenteral nutrition to ensure that patients receive adequate levels of this vital mineral.\",490\r\n4693,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,ZINC,\"NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL is a medical practice that involves providing essential nutrients directly into the bloodstream, bypassing the digestive system. One of the key components included in NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL is ZINC, which is recognized as an essential trace element. ZINC is particularly recommended in pediatric parenteral nutrition to ensure that the nutritional needs of children are adequately met. It plays a crucial role in fulfilling the body's trace element requirements, thereby supporting overall health and development in patients receiving parenteral nutrition.\",490\r\n4680,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,HIERRO,\"NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL, which refers to the intravenous administration of nutrients, often includes the essential oligoelemento, HIERRO (iron). While the use of iron in parenteral nutrition is considered essential, it remains a subject of controversy. It is crucial to monitor iron levels and add it independently in parenteral nutrition to prevent deficiencies, particularly for patients who require this form of nutrition for extended periods. Therefore, iron supplementation is necessary to ensure the health and well-being of individuals receiving parenteral nutrition.\",483\r\n4635,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,INSUFICIENCIA RENAL,\"NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL is a specialized form of nutrition that is utilized in cases of INSUFICIENCIA RENAL, particularly when the gastrointestinal tract is not functional. In such scenarios, parenteral nutrition becomes essential to provide the necessary nutrients and fluids that the body requires. Insuficiencia renal necessitates specific adjustments in the administration of parenteral nutrition to prevent potential complications. These adjustments may include careful management of fluid and nutrient intake to accommodate the altered physiological needs of patients with renal insufficiency. Overall, parenteral nutrition serves as a critical intervention for individuals with severe renal insufficiency when traditional nutritional methods are not viable.\",479\r\n4755,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,CIRUGÍA BARIÁTRICA,La nutrición parenteral puede ser necesaria en el postoperatorio de cirugía bariátrica si el paciente no puede alimentarse adecuadamente,479\r\n4335,ASPEN,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,\"ASPEN (American Society for Parenteral and Enteral Nutrition) establishes comprehensive guidelines regarding the use of parenteral nutrition for various patient conditions. Specifically, ASPEN provides recommendations for the administration of parenteral nutrition in patients suffering from pancreatitis, as well as those experiencing severe diarrhea and other related conditions. Additionally, ASPEN emphasizes the importance of parenteral nutrition for patients who are unable to receive nourishment through the digestive tract. These guidelines aim to ensure that patients receive appropriate nutritional support tailored to their specific medical needs.\",479\r\n4649,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,GLUTAMINA,\"NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL refers to the method of providing nutrition to patients intravenously, bypassing the usual process of eating and digestion. Within this context, GLUTAMINA, or glutamine, is recognized as an important nutrient. It is recommended as part of the nutritional support in parenteral nutrition for patients, particularly those experiencing metabolic stress. Research indicates that glutamine can improve clinical outcomes for these patients, making it a valuable supplement in their nutritional therapy.\n\nSpecifically, glutamine is advised for use in parenteral nutrition to enhance recovery in patients with acute pancreatitis. Additionally, it has been shown to support glycemic control in diabetic patients when included in their nutritional regimen. Overall, glutamine plays a significant role in optimizing the effectiveness of parenteral nutrition, contributing to better health outcomes for a variety of patient populations.\",472\r\n4914,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,AMERICAN SOCIETY FOR PARENTERAL AND ENTERAL NUTRITION,\"ASPEN provides guidelines for the practice of parenteral nutrition, particularly in pediatric patients\",472\r\n4610,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,SÍNDROME DE INTESTINO CORTO,\"NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL and SÍNDROME DE INTESTINO CORTO are closely related in the context of medical treatment for patients suffering from the latter condition. Síndrome de intestino corto, characterized by a significant reduction in the functional length of the intestine, often leads to severe malabsorption of nutrients. As a result, patients with this syndrome frequently require nutrición parenteral to ensure they receive adequate nutrition. This form of nutrition is essential for those who cannot absorb sufficient nutrients through their intestines, making it a common and sometimes necessary treatment option.\n\nIn cases of severe síndrome de intestino corto, nutrición parenteral is considered an absolute indication, highlighting its critical role in managing the nutritional needs of affected individuals. The reliance on parenteral nutrition may be long-term, as the malabsorption issues associated with this syndrome complicate the ability to meet nutritional requirements through conventional dietary means. Overall, nutrición parenteral serves as a vital intervention for patients with síndrome de intestino corto, addressing their unique challenges related to nutrient absorption.\",471\r\n4719,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,VITAMINA B12,Vitamin B12 is included in parenteral nutrition to support nerve function,471\r\n4759,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,QUILOTÓRAX,\"NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL is utilized in cases of QUILOTÓRAX, particularly when enteral nutrition is insufficient or not feasible. This form of nutrition is indicated for patients suffering from quilotórax who are experiencing significant nutritional deficiencies, ensuring that their dietary needs are met when traditional methods are inadequate.\",471\r\n4750,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL (NP),Parenteral nutrition is a method of providing nutrients when enteral nutrition is inadequate,469\r\n4788,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,SIC,\"Patients with SIC typically need nutritional support, often through parenteral means\",468\r\n4816,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,TRASPLANTE DE CÉLULAS HEMATOLÓGICAS,La nutrición parenteral es un método de soporte nutricional que puede ser requerido en el contexto del trasplante de células hematológicas,468\r\n4715,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,VITAMINA E,Vitamin E is included in parenteral nutrition to protect cells from oxidative stress,466\r\n4756,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,INSUFICIENCIA RENAL AGUDA,\"NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL is a medical intervention that may be necessary for patients suffering from INSUFICIENCIA RENAL AGUDA, particularly when these individuals require intensive nutritional support. This form of nutrition is utilized when enteral feeding is not feasible, making it a critical option for managing the nutritional needs of patients experiencing acute renal failure.\",466\r\n4632,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,HIPERTRIGLICERIDEMIA,\"NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL refers to a method of providing nutrition to individuals who cannot consume food orally, typically through intravenous means. One of the potential complications associated with NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL is HIPERTRIGLICERIDEMIA, which can arise if the lipid intake during parenteral nutrition is not adequately managed. Specifically, HIPERTRIGLICERIDEMIA can occur as a direct result of lipid administration in parenteral nutrition, highlighting the importance of careful monitoring and control of lipid levels to prevent this condition.\",462\r\n4803,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,CÁNCER GÁSTRICO,\"La nutrición parenteral es un tratamiento esencial para pacientes con cáncer gástrico, especialmente en aquellos que presentan malnutrición. Se utiliza en situaciones donde la nutrición enteral no es viable, proporcionando una alternativa crucial para asegurar que estos pacientes reciban los nutrientes necesarios. En particular, la nutrición parenteral domiciliaria complementaria se aplica en casos de cáncer gástrico avanzado, ayudando a mejorar la calidad de vida y el estado nutricional de los pacientes en esta etapa crítica de la enfermedad.\",460\r\n4696,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,SELENIO,Selenium is included in parenteral nutrition to meet the body's trace element requirements,458\r\n4721,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,\"DIETOTERAPIA, NUTRICIÓN CLÍNICA Y METABOLISMO\",The book discusses parenteral nutrition as part of clinical nutrition and metabolism,458\r\n4682,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,FÓSFORO,\"NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL, which refers to the intravenous administration of nutrients, is critically dependent on the inclusion of FÓSFORO (phosphorus) as an essential component. Phosphorus is necessary for the proper development of pediatric patients, making it a vital supplement in their parenteral nutrition regimen. It plays a crucial role in meeting the body's mineral requirements, and its levels are carefully adjusted based on the individual needs of each patient. Overall, phosphorus is recognized as an indispensable nutrient that must be incorporated into parenteral nutrition to ensure optimal health outcomes for patients, particularly in pediatric care.\",457\r\n1474,ENFERMEDAD DE CROHN,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,La enfermedad de Crohn puede causar malnutrición y requerir nutrición parenteral en casos severos donde la alimentación oral no es suficiente.,457\r\n2125,GASTROENTEROLOGY,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,Gastroenterology studies often include research on the effectiveness of parenteral nutrition in treating digestive disorders.,456\r\n4663,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,HIPERGLUCEMIA,\"NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL and HIPERGLUCEMIA are closely related, as hyperglycemia is a potential complication that can arise from improper management of parenteral nutrition. It is frequently observed in patients undergoing NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL, making it a common concern in this context. Effective management of hyperglycemia is essential during nutritional therapy, particularly for diabetic patients, to prevent further complications. Therefore, careful monitoring and adjustment of nutritional strategies are crucial to mitigate the risk of HIPERGLUCEMIA in individuals receiving NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL.\",454\r\n4805,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,CÁNCER DE ESÓFAGO,La nutrición parenteral puede ser necesaria en pacientes con cáncer de esófago que no pueden alimentarse adecuadamente.,454\r\n4843,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,COPPER,Copper levels should be reduced in parenteral nutrition to avoid toxicity,454\r\n4441,SÍNDROME DE REALIMENTACIÓN,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,\"The Síndrome de Realimentación, or Refeeding Syndrome, is a significant risk associated with Nutrición Parenteral, particularly in patients who are severely malnourished. This syndrome can occur if parenteral nutrition is not managed properly, as the reintroduction of feeding in these vulnerable patients can lead to serious complications. It is crucial to handle parenteral nutrition with care to prevent the onset of refeeding syndrome, which can arise from the rapid changes in metabolism that occur when feeding is resumed.\",454\r\n4931,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,AMINOVEN INFANT®,Aminoven Infant® es una solución utilizada en la nutrición parenteral pediátrica para proporcionar aminoácidos esenciales a los infantes,453\r\n4937,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,RNPT,RNPT es un grupo de pacientes que se beneficia de la nutrición parenteral debido a su condición de recién nacidos pretérmino,452\r\n903,RADIOTERAPIA,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,Radiotherapy can cause side effects that necessitate the use of parenteral nutrition,452\r\n4624,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,CER-NEVIT,CER-NEVIT is a multivitamin composition used in parenteral nutrition,451\r\n4691,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,SMOFLIPID,\"NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL refers to the method of providing nutrition intravenously to patients who are unable to consume food orally or through the gastrointestinal tract. SMOFLIPID is a specific lipid emulsion utilized within this context. It is designed to offer a balanced source of lipids, which includes essential omega-3 fatty acids, thereby enhancing the nutritional support provided through parenteral nutrition. SMOFLIPID plays a crucial role in ensuring that patients receive the necessary fats for their health and recovery when traditional feeding methods are not viable.\",451\r\n4710,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,TIAMINA,Thiamine is included in parenteral nutrition to support metabolic processes,451\r\n4911,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,PACIENTE PEDIÁTRICO,La nutrición parenteral es un tratamiento utilizado específicamente para pacientes pediátricos que no pueden alimentarse adecuadamente.,451\r\n4809,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,PACIENTES ONCOLÓGICOS,La nutrición parenteral puede ser necesaria para pacientes oncológicos con fallo intestinal,450\r\n4690,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,LIPOFUNDINA,\"NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL refers to a method of providing nutrition to individuals who cannot obtain adequate nutrition through oral intake. Within this context, LIPOFUNDINA is a lipid emulsion specifically utilized in parenteral nutrition. It serves as a vital component by supplying a source of energy and essential fatty acids, which are crucial for maintaining the nutritional needs of patients receiving parenteral nutrition.\",449\r\n4700,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,RECIÉN NACIDOS PREMATUROS,Preterm infants are the primary beneficiaries of parenteral nutrition to prevent undernutrition,449\r\n4932,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,PRIMENE®,Primene® es una solución utilizada en la nutrición parenteral pediátrica para proporcionar aminoácidos esenciales a los niños,448\r\n4988,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,SMOFKABIVEN CENTRAL,SmofKabiven Central is used in the event of parenteral nutrition,448\r\n4662,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,CROMO,\"NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL involves the administration of nutrients directly into the bloodstream, often used for patients who cannot consume food orally. CROMO, or chromium, is an oligoelement that plays a role in various metabolic processes. While chromium supplementation may aid in improving glycemic control and insulin sensitivity in diabetic patients undergoing nutritional therapy, it is important to note that chromium can be nefrotóxico (toxic to the kidneys) in neonates, necessitating careful monitoring of its administration in this vulnerable population. Therefore, while chromium has potential benefits in specific contexts, its use must be approached with caution, particularly in neonates receiving parenteral nutrition.\",447\r\n4687,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,CLORO,\"NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL, which refers to parenteral nutrition, includes CLORO, or chloride, as an essential electrolyte. Chloride plays a crucial role in the formulation of parenteral nutrition solutions, particularly for pediatric patients. It is necessary for fluid regulation within the body, highlighting its importance in maintaining electrolyte balance and overall health in individuals receiving parenteral nutrition.\",447\r\n4840,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,TABLA 3,\"NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL is supported by TABLA 3, which offers essential information regarding nitrogen and glucose solutions utilized in parenteral nutrition. Additionally, TABLA 3 outlines guidelines for monitoring clinical parameters in patients who are receiving parenteral nutrition, ensuring that healthcare providers can effectively manage and assess the nutritional needs and health status of these patients.\",447\r\n4928,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,LIPOPLUS,Lipoplus is used in parenteral nutrition to deliver essential fatty acids and support metabolic needs,447\r\n4648,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,FRA,Parenteral nutrition is necessary for patients with acute renal failure when enteral nutrition is insufficient or not possible.,446\r\n4694,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,COBRE,Copper is included in parenteral nutrition to meet the body's trace element requirements,445\r\n4731,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,FOSFATO,\"NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL, which refers to the intravenous administration of nutrients, relies on various components to ensure effective metabolic support. One such component is FOSFATO, or phosphate, which is essential for numerous metabolic functions. While phosphate is included in parenteral nutrition solutions, it necessitates careful management to prevent potential complications associated with its use. Thus, the incorporation of FOSFATO in NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL is vital, but it must be monitored closely to maintain patient safety and health.\",445\r\n4745,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,INSUFICIENCIA HEPÁTICA,Insuficiencia hepática necessitates careful management of lipid intake in parenteral nutrition,445\r\n4938,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,RNT,RNT es un grupo de pacientes que también puede requerir nutrición parenteral en caso de no poder alimentarse adecuadamente,445\r\n4851,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,INSULINA REGULAR,Insulina regular is commonly administered within the context of nutrición parenteral to manage blood glucose levels,444\r\n4729,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,AMINOÁCIDOS,\"NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL involves the use of AMINOÁCIDOS, which are essential components in parenteral solutions. These amino acids play a critical role in providing nutrition to patients who cannot receive food through traditional means. They are vital for meeting patients' protein requirements, maintaining body mass, and supporting protein synthesis. In summary, amino acids are key ingredients in the formulation of parenteral nutrition, delivering essential nutrients to patients in need.\",443\r\n4641,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,SÍNDROME DE DISTRÉS RESPIRATORIO AGUDO,Nutrición parenteral is often recommended for patients suffering from síndrome de distrés respiratorio agudo to meet their increased nutritional needs.,443\r\n4711,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,RIBOFLAVINA,Riboflavin is included in parenteral nutrition to aid in energy production,443\r\n4718,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,BIOTINA,Biotin is included in parenteral nutrition to support metabolism,443\r\n4923,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,CARNITINA,Carnitine is often considered for inclusion in parenteral nutrition solutions to aid in lipid clearance,443\r\n4992,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,ACETATO,Acetato is used in parenteral nutrition solutions to help maintain acid-base balance,443\r\n4592,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,B. BALERDI PÉREZ,\"B. Balerdi Pérez is an author who has contributed to the chapter on Parenteral Nutrition, focusing on the methods and indications associated with this nutritional approach.\",442\r\n4860,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,ENFERMEDAD HEPÁTICA,\"NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL refers to a method of providing nutrition to patients intravenously, bypassing the usual process of eating and digestion. This approach can be beneficial in managing patients with ENFERMEDAD 